Step 5 — the full reverse


    Processing

      ▶ Run
      ⏸ Pause



    int[] values = { 30, 80, 45, 120, 60, 95, 40 };

void setup() {
  size(400, 200);
}

void draw() {
  background(240);
  int barWidth = width / values.length;
  for (int i = 0; i &lt; values.length; i++) {
    fill(70, 150, 110);
    noStroke();
    rect(i * barWidth, height - values[i], barWidth - 4, values[i]);
  }
}

void mousePressed() {
  reverseArray();
}

void reverseArray() {
  for (int i = 0; i &lt; values.length / 2; i++) {
    int temp = values[i];
    values[i] = values[values.length - 1 - i];
    values[values.length - 1 - i] = temp;
  }
}





    Errors



Same swap as Step 4, now looped from both ends toward the middle — the full reverse algorithm. The loop only needs to go halfway (i &lt; values.length / 2) because each swap handles a pair of elements at once — running it the full length would just swap everything back to where it started.

