Common Mistakes

Four mistakes that appear frequently in this unit. The precedence mistake (mixing && and || without parentheses) produces wrong results that compile fine — hardest to spot. The ordering mistake causes unreachable branches. The off-by-one in else if is subtle (&gt;= vs &gt; for grade boundaries). Using nested if when else if would be cleaner makes code harder to read.

1. Mixing && and || without parentheses
// Intended: (isStudent || isSenior) && hasId
// Actual:   isStudent || (isSenior && hasId)  ← different!
if (isStudent || isSenior && hasId) { ... }

// Fix — always parenthesize when mixing:
if ((isStudent || isSenior) && hasId) { ... }
2. else if conditions in the wrong order — unreachable branches
if (score &gt;= 60) { IO.println("D"); }        // too broad — catches everyone
else if (score &gt;= 90) { IO.println("A"); }   // unreachable!

// Fix — most specific first:
if (score &gt;= 90) { IO.println("A"); }
else if (score &gt;= 60) { IO.println("D"); }
3. Using &gt; instead of &gt;= at grade boundaries
if (score &gt; 90) { IO.println("A"); }   // misses exactly 90
if (score &gt;= 90) { IO.println("A"); }  // ✓
4. Deep nesting when else if or && would be cleaner
// Overly nested — hard to follow
if (age &gt;= 18) {
    if (score &gt;= 60) {
        if (homeworkDone) {
            IO.println("Pass");
        }
    }
}

// Cleaner with &&
if (age &gt;= 18 && score &gt;= 60 && homeworkDone) {
    IO.println("Pass");
}

